---
title: "Radiographic Procedures II"
code: "RAD-221"
category: "radiography"
credits: "4"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/RAD-110"
  - "2026/RAD-121"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisites: RAD 110 and RAD 121"
---

Continues procedures for positioning the patient’s anatomical structures relative to x-ray beam and image receptor. Emphasizes procedures for routine examination of the skull, contrast studies of internal organs, and special procedures employed in the more complicated investigation of the human body. Lecture 3 hours, Laboratory 3 hours, Total 6 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
